Z||000000||gomobile||09-19-2001||03:46 PM||||I have notice that once in awhile when I open the Passenger door it hits the fender where that puppy almost belts in? Any ideas why? The door seems to be align properly. BUT then again I am not an expert on the BODY. ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Hank is Here||09-19-2001||03:50 PM||||Are your hinge pins worn?||||reg||1
Z||000002||gomobile||09-19-2001||04:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hank is Here:<BR><B>Are your hinge pins worn?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I replaced the HINGE pins. But this was happening prior to replacement. So I am a little baffle?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||09-19-2001||04:21 PM||||Here is a situation I had with the same results:<BR>I was installing foglights and in the process of running the wires I leaned on the front fender.  I did not notice anything until i went to close the front door and found that it now had contact with the fender!I stuck a long screwdriver with a sock on the shaft in and pryed a tiny bit.  Now its fine.  You could not even tell it was out of position it was so fine.  Try it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-19-2001||07:23 PM||||The way the door skins are mounted means they have a certain amount of "float" in their mounting hardware. There is a small amount of front/rear movement possible.<P>If the prying method above doesn't work (be carfull you don't crack a pannel) then loosen door skin hardware, including the 2 screws under the trim. Then try a bit of prying.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||09-19-2001||08:45 PM||||or you can loosen the fender mounting bolts inside the front hood along the edge and move it forwards or outward slightly. Check the rear edge gap on door first, if you have plenty there, slide the door skin back slightly instead.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChopTop||09-20-2001||08:52 AM||||It will do this on my car when it's hot outside, I'm assuming urethane expands when hot.  I'll deal with adjustng the door panel when I have the car painted.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||gomobile||09-20-2001||11:20 AM||||To all I will try some these ideas this weekend. After all I will be adding new window DEWS. So I will have to play with the skins and such.||||reg||6
Z||000008||fldevel||09-20-2001||05:22 PM||||note:all body panles MOVE and are ajustible bolts may have come loose on door panels or fender ..i had a simular problem when i took all my pannels off to have the car painted and when i replaced them it seemed like nothign fit properly and i had to do some major ajusting ..hope this helps ||||reg||1
